    "created_at": "2024-01-16T16:48:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-01-16T16:48:58Z",
    "body": "Hi @KilianPoirier, @vishal-ph and @shahidee44. Here is an update on the project: \r\n\r\n1.  We managed to create a wrapper for ZNE. You can check the current version [here](https://github.com/victor-onofre/openqaoa/blob/dev/src/openqaoa-core/openqaoa/backends/wrapper.py). At the moment the code is messy but we will improve it during the rest of the tests. \r\n\r\n2. We have some preliminary results with a random instance of the Max-Cut problem using noise models. These results are unoptimized, but they show the wrapper is working. [Here](https://github.com/victor-onofre/openqaoa/blob/dev/src/openqaoa-core/Adriano_Results/9-1-24/exp1/conditions.txt), you can check the parameters of the simulation. Here is a cost history plot of the results:\r\n![3 2qaoa_qaoanoise_qaoazne_maxcut_cost](https://github.com/entropicalabs/openqaoa/assets/62406347/882f544c-9889-4c97-b60c-e377e37b084e)\r\n3. We are currently working on benchmarking with the Max cut and Knapsack problem (Obtaining optimal solution in a noiseless simulation and then applying the noise model to find the optimal parameters of the ZNE method ) ",
